  "summary": "Reverse shell on require to 66.78.40.218:32768",
  "details": "The gem's library entry point opens a TCP connection to the hardcoded remote host 66.78.40.218 on port 32768, reopens STDIN, STDOUT, and STDERR onto the socket, and execs /bin/sh -i. Any process that requires this gem immediately hands an interactive shell on the installer's host, running as the installer's user, to whoever controls that IP. The behavior fires unconditionally at module load, has no authentication, no gating, and no legitimate relationship to the gem's self-described purpose.",
